<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
The device admin's policies (keep/AdminReceiver): none, on purpose, as in
proof five. An active device admin cannot be uninstalled until it is switched
off in Settings, which is all the base protection asks of it, and a device
owner needs no policy here for what strict mode does. An empty list means
Android refuses this admin the old powers: wiping the phone, resetting or
changing the screen lock, locking the screen, switching off the camera or
features of the lock screen.
-->
<device-admin>
    <uses-policies />
</device-admin>
